 "limitations": [
  "I-24 critical gaps come from partial tracking (about 0.5-0.65 of peak vehicle-time); under coverage thinning of complete US-101 the critical gaps are undetermined (lead +0.10 s, lag +0.17 / +0.39 s at F = 0.65 / 0.5; B\u00a71 coverage rules). The us101_gaps arm is the complete-coverage check.",
  "25-35 % of I-24 drivers are inconsistent with the one-threshold driver model the joint estimator assumes (WP-78); the fits are central values, not thresholds.",
  "tau_r is the only supported relaxation fit (176 US-101 leader sides); no follower side fit is supported in either dataset (B\u00a71.4).",
  "delta rests on the entering partner speeds; the exiting movement uses the weave's delta (docs/MERGE_MODEL.md \u00a72 gives one delta per zone kind)."
 ]
}
